Key Takeaway

Azure Virtual Networks provide the foundation for secure communication between Azure resources. By properly planning address spaces, creating subnets, and managing public and private IP addressing, Azure Administrators can build scalable, secure, and highly available cloud networking environments that support both internal workloads and internet-facing applications.
